          "outcome": {
            "summary": "One-line change replaces exact == with fabs(actual - r) < 1e-12 for all nine captured values. math.h is already included (line 21); formatting (tabs, operator spacing) matches the file; unit check passed on 4695c139a. Tolerance: 1e-12 deg is ~6x the measured max Moon deviation (1.6e-13 deg) on Linux x86_64, so it is not flaky, and it equals 3.6e-9 arcsec, i.e. a relative 1e-9 on the ~1e-3 deg nutation values and far below the 0.001 arcsec effects the comment names as meaningful, so changes to nutation, Sun and Moon are still detected. Observations only (out of scope): the test name and comment still say bit-for-bit; the fprintf on any != now prints diagnostic noise for passing ulp-level differences; ASSERT_NEAR from test_runner.h would be an equivalent alternative.",
